===========================================================================
Third-party notices
===========================================================================

1) EurySPACE CCSDS RX/TX library  --  rtl/ccsds_rxtx/
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Project : EurySPACE CCSDS RX/TX with wishbone interface
   Author  : Guillaume REMBERT
   Licence : MIT          (stated in the header of every source file)

   MIT is compatible with this repository's MIT licence, so the library may
   be redistributed and modified freely, provided the original copyright
   notice is retained. The headers in the affected files are kept intact.

   Modules REWRITTEN or FIXED by this project (see the header comment inside
   each file for the exact reasoning and measurements):

     ccsds_rxtx_srrc.vhd
         Rewritten from scratch. The original "pipelined systolic symmetric"
         implementation used a `variable` accumulator inside a `for` loop,
         which ModelSim simulates correctly but Vivado synthesises with a
         completely different result: the output saturated at +/-128 and
         changing the output shift from 7 to 9 produced no change on hardware.
         The rewrite uses only signals, an explicit resize at each adder
         stage, symmetric pre-adders (31 multipliers instead of 61), and a
         single arithmetic shift plus explicit saturation at the output.
         Generated by sim/gen_srrc_signals.py.

     ccsds_rxtx_clock_divider.vhd
         Fixed. For DIVIDER = 1 the original produced
             clk_o <= clk_i and (not rst_i);
         i.e. a combinational gated clock built from an asynchronous enable,
         which glitches after synthesis. Changed to pass the clock through
         directly and let each sub-module handle its own synchronous reset.

   The remaining files in rtl/ccsds_rxtx/ are unmodified upstream sources
   and keep their original MIT headers.

2) ADI no-OS AD9361 driver  --  referenced by the relay-board firmware
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   ad9361.c / ad9361_api.c / ad9361.h / ad9361_api.h are derived from the
   Analog Devices no-OS AD9361 driver (ADI BSD-style licence). They are NOT
   redistributed in this repository. The new Z7ADDALite application sources
   are standalone C code; external BSP/driver sources are described below.

3) Analog Devices HDL reference design
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   The vendor material pack referenced in the documentation contains the
   ADI HDL reference components (axi_ad9361, axi_dmac, axi_clkgen, ...).
   Those files are NOT redistributed here.

   The separate AD9643 PN9 reference is redistributed at:
   board/z7addalite/telecontrol_system/reference/axi_ad9643_pnmon_2016_r1.v
   Source: Analog Devices hdl, tag hdl_2016_r1,
   library/axi_ad9643/axi_ad9643_pnmon.v.
   Its original copyright, redistribution conditions (including the ADI
   component condition), and disclaimer are retained in the file. They are
   not replaced by this project's MIT licence. It documents the PN sequence
   used to check the AD9643 data interface.

4) AMD/Xilinx tools, BSP and board configuration
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Vivado IP, generated BSP libraries and the embeddedsw 2018.3 source archive
   are external build dependencies, not bundled libraries in this repository.
   The preparation scripts retain the upstream notices when extracting the
   source subset. Generated or modified vendor code remains subject to its
   original licence; the project licence does not relicense it.

   board/z7addalite/telecontrol_system/vendor/zynq_petaLinux.bd is a PS7
   configuration input from the board material's PetaLinux boot example,
   petaLinux20183_vivado.zip (Vivado 2018.3).
   It provides the board DDR/MIO settings, not a Linux image or BSP.
   No separate licence was included with that configuration in the supplied
   board material; no additional licence grant for vendor material is implied.

===========================================================================
CCSDS standard notice
===========================================================================

The protocol implementation follows:

  * CCSDS 131.0-B  TM Synchronization and Channel Coding
  * CCSDS 133.0-B  Space Packet Protocol

The CCSDS recommendations themselves are published by the Consultative
Committee for Space Data Systems and are not redistributed here. Only this
project's independent implementation of the described formats is included.
